{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Patch set 3 of Gerrit 3427 (commit 6dfd8c97650, same Change-Id). It acts on the 4 LLM-Review advisories from patch set 2:\n1. The survivor-diagnosis re-run (_diagnose_non_killed) also executes mutated code in the bwrap sandbox, so it now gets TMPDIR=basetemp too.\n2. test_shard_children_get_a_writable_temp_dir now drives both sandboxed children (clean run, then mutmut run) and asserts TMPDIR on both. New test_survivor_diagnosis_gets_a_writable_temp_dir covers point 1. Both fail with the TMPDIR lines removed.\n3. file_impact now lists scripts/mutation_gate.py, tests/scripts/test_mutation_gate.py and .joe-janitor/tools.md.\n4. .joe-janitor/tools.md no longer describes the marker as the literal /tmp path.\n\nPatch set 2's Verified -1 came from tests/unit/test_model_classes.py::test_a_finished_gate_drive_releases_its_event_loop[raised] on py3.11 and py3.12 (run 44429902115). That test is tracked as unselfish-finnicky-whooper and is not touched by this change; the same test passed on 3430 patch set 2, whose tree includes this commit. Local reproduction on anyio 4.16.0: the per-run loop was still alive right after gc.collect() in 32 of 400 drives, and all 32 were freed within 0.5 s. That supports the delayed-release explanation recorded on that ticket."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1795051322773236803,"uuid":"2fcc3488-436d-4520-a7cb-1602c524c1c8"}